From: Lucas Santos <lsantos7654@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Apr 2026 01:11:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 20/20] Tests: presence + focus model
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Six bun:test cases in `test/server/event.test.ts` exercising the
per-client presence/focus state machine end-to-end via Hono's
`app.request()` (no real port, no Bun.serve listener):

  1. SSE without `X-Client-ID` is a no-op for liveness.
  2. SSE with `X-Client-ID` registers the client; focus stays null
     until POST /event/focus.
  3. POST /event/focus updates the live set; the focused sessionID
     appears in `/global/live-sessions.sessions`.
  4. Cancelling the SSE stream removes the client from the live
     set within ~50ms (the leak-catcher — regression here is
     exactly the bug class the prior 11 patches chased).
  5. POST /event/focus without a prior SSE returns 404.
  6. Two clients with distinct focuses; cancelling one drops only
     that client's focus from the live set.

`stream.onAbort` is the canonical disconnect hook on Bun >= 1.2,
and `app.request()` exercises it via the response body's
ReadableStream cancel — so these tests run the same code path
that production fetch / TCP-close drives, without needing a real
HTTP listener.

A small `readSSE(stream)` helper at the top of the file pulls
`data:` lines off `text/event-stream` chunks and JSON-parses each
event. Tests use `nextOfType` (not yet) / `next` to walk past
`server.connected` sentinels and assert on bus events.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 packages/opencode/test/server/event.test.ts | 220 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 220 insertions(+)
